From 5f942fb1075f406a47eb531e429e3c3afa414334 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: faycal <faycalelhandi9@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:13:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 30/35] feat(hybrid): opt-in DLSS Frame Generation through
 Streamline

ASTROHYBRID_DLSSG=1 (with a KYTY_STREAMLINE_DIR build) initialises
Streamline before the Vulkan instance and takes Vulkan from
sl.interposer.dll; the window surface is created through it so DLSS-G
finds the window. Per guest frame: Streamline Reflex sleep and latency
markers on the existing frame hooks, the game's camera from its per-view
constants, depth and motion vectors tagged at the temporal upscale pass,
and constants with previous-frame matrices. ASTROHYBRID_DLSSG_FRAMES
selects the generated frames, clamped to the runtime's maximum. Also:
the pass trace can scan bound buffers for projection matrices, and DLSS
SR now defaults to non-inverted depth as the game's projection shows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
